course: dictionary
lesson: 3480
title: Falsely
level: primary-5
stars: 3
explain: Falsely is an adverb. It tells you how something is done, and it means in a way that is not true or not correct. «She falsely accused him» means she said he did something wrong, but he did not.
explain: Read the clues around the word. «He was put in prison» tells you he was blamed for something he did not do. So falsely must mean untruly, and the blame was wrong. Check it by swapping in another word: «wrongly accused» still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
explain: Falsely can also mean pretend, not sincere. A falsely cheerful voice sounds happy, but the speaker does not really feel happy. The clue is in the word cheerful: it sounds like a happy voice, but the feeling is not real.
fact: Falsely is an adverb: it tells you how something is done.
fact: «Falsely» means in a way that is not true or not correct.
fact: «Falsely accused» means blamed for something you did not do.
fact: «Falsely cheerful» means pretending to be happy when you are not.
fact: A good check is to swap in «wrongly» or «untruly» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: In Egypt, Joseph was put in prison after «she falsely accused him». What does falsely mean here? | *Not true, so he was blamed for something he did not do | Happily and with a big smile | Very loudly, so everyone heard
exercise: «In a team, blaming a teammate falsely can get him left out.» Which word could replace falsely with almost the same meaning? | Kindly | Proudly | Slowly | *Wrongly
exercise: Ella says a «falsely cheerful voice» sounds happy. What is the real feeling behind it? | The speaker is singing a song | *The speaker is pretending to be happy | The speaker is really over the moon
test: Sam falsely claims he won the race, but he came last. What does falsely mean? | *Says something that is not true | Loudly and proudly | Fast and clever
test: Why is being falsely blamed unfair? | Because the person was the best at the game | Because the blame was loud | *Because the person did not do what they are blamed for
exam: Which sentence uses falsely to mean pretend, not sincere? | The tree fell falsely in the storm | *The boy gave a falsely cheerful smile, hiding how sad he felt | The cat sat falsely on the mat
